IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc5-logic`
IMPORT `ssc5-part7`
IMPORT `ssc5-part9`

-- Tests for ssc5-part9.l4 (ss 141 to 147).  Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the
-- section named beside it, before the run.
-- 1 December 2025 was a Monday; every date below is counted from it.

§ `Tests -- Part IX`

§§ `s 147(1) -- "week" begins on a Monday`

-- Monday 1 December 2025: the week is 1 to 7 December.
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 1 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 1 12 2025
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 1 12 2025))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 7 12 2025
-- Wednesday 3 December 2025.
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 3 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 1 12 2025
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 3 12 2025))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 7 12 2025
-- Sunday 7 December 2025 belongs to the week that began on Monday 1 December.
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 7 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 1 12 2025
-- Monday 8 December 2025 starts the next week.
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 8 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 8 12 2025
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 8 12 2025))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 14 12 2025
-- Saturday 6 December 2025.
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 6 12 2025))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 1 12 2025
-- A week across a year end: Thursday 1 January 2026 is in the week of Monday 29 December 2025.
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 1 1 2026))'s `the first day` EQUALS Date 29 12 2025
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) the week containing the date` (Date 1 1 2026))'s `the last day` EQUALS Date 4 1 2026

§§ `s 147(1) -- "voluntary organisation" and "prescribed"`

-- A body other than a public or local authority whose activities are carried on otherwise than for profit.
#ASSERT `s 147(1) the body is a voluntary organisation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 147(1) the body is a voluntary organisation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 147(1) the body is a voluntary organisation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 147(1) the body is a voluntary organisation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT (`s 147(1) how the term is defined` `s 147(1) prescribed`)'s `what it points at or says` EQUALS "prescribed by regulations"
#ASSERT (`s 147(1) how the term is defined` `s 147(1) prescribed`)'s `the way it is defined` EQUALS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`

§§ `s 147(2) -- a condition or fact "in a week" is judged at the beginning of the week`

#ASSERT `s 147(2) the day on which a condition or fact in the week is judged` (Date 1 12 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 12 2025)
-- "Subject to any provision made by regulations": a provision in regulations points outside the text.
#ASSERT `s 147(2) the day on which a condition or fact in the week is judged` (Date 1 12 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 147(3) -- step-relations`

#ASSERT `s 147(3) the person is within a reference in this Part to a parent, father or mother` `s 147(3) a step-parent` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 147(3) the person is within a reference in this Part to a parent, father or mother` `s 147(3) a step-father` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 147(3) the person is within a reference in this Part to a parent, father or mother` `s 147(3) a step-mother` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "including": the list is not closed, so another relation is not answered no.
#ASSERT `s 147(3) the person is within a reference in this Part to a parent, father or mother` `s 147(3) some other relation` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 147(6) -- no right for a body corporate`

-- A body corporate, and no regulations conferring the right: the text says no in its own words.
#ASSERT `s 147(6) this Part confers a right to child benefit on the body` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "but regulations may confer such a right on voluntary organisations": that points outside the text.
#ASSERT `s 147(6) this Part confers a right to child benefit on the body` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a body corporate: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 147(6) this Part confers a right to child benefit on the body` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 147(6) this Part confers a right to child benefit on the body` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 142 -- "child" and "qualifying young person"`

-- (1): the answer is the one s 173(a) gives for "under 16".
#ASSERT `s 142(1) the person is a child` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 142(1) the person is a child` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 142(1) the person is a child` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2): other than a child, below the prescribed age, and the prescribed conditions are satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A child is excluded by "other than a child".
#ASSERT `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not below the prescribed age.
#ASSERT `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Prescribed conditions not satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The age comes from regulations: unknown stays unknown.
#ASSERT `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A known no on one limb beats an unknown on another.
#ASSERT `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 143(3) -- days of absence that are disregarded`

-- Arguments: the reason; whether the absence is due solely to it; for reason (c), whether the circumstances are prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 143(3) the day of absence is disregarded` `s 143(3)(a) receiving education or training of a description prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(3) the day of absence is disregarded` `s 143(3)(b) undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(3) the day of absence is disregarded` `s 143(3)(c) in residential accommodation pursuant to arrangements made under one of the Acts listed, in prescribed circumstances` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) without prescribed circumstances.
#ASSERT `s 143(3) the day of absence is disregarded` `s 143(3)(c) in residential accommodation pursuant to arrangements made under one of the Acts listed, in prescribed circumstances` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not due solely to the fact.
#ASSERT `s 143(3) the day of absence is disregarded` `s 143(3)(a) receiving education or training of a description prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Some other reason: the three listed reasons are not said to be the only ones.
#ASSERT `s 143(3) the day of absence is disregarded` `s 143(3) some other reason` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 143(4) -- the limit on days disregarded under (3)(b) or (c)`

-- Arguments: days under (3)(a); days under (3)(b) or (c); the prescribed number; whether expenditure is regularly incurred.
#ASSERT `s 143(4) the number of days that may be disregarded` 5 30 20 FALSE EQUALS 25
-- Regular expenditure lifts the limit.
#ASSERT `s 143(4) the number of days that may be disregarded` 5 30 20 TRUE EQUALS 35
-- Under the limit.
#ASSERT `s 143(4) the number of days that may be disregarded` 0 10 20 FALSE EQUALS 10
-- Exactly at the limit: "shall not exceed" allows it.
#ASSERT `s 143(4) the number of days that may be disregarded` 5 20 20 FALSE EQUALS 25
-- A limit of nothing allows nothing under (b) or (c) but still allows (a).
#ASSERT `s 143(4) the number of days that may be disregarded` 7 3 0 FALSE EQUALS 7

§§ `s 143(2) -- absence for more than 56 days in the 16 weeks`

-- Arguments: the person has had the child living with him before; days absent in the 16 weeks; days to be disregarded.
#ASSERT `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` TRUE 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Exactly 56 days is not "more than 56".
#ASSERT `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` TRUE 56 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` TRUE 57 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Disregarded days are not counted: 70 less 14 is 56, and 70 less 13 is 57.
#ASSERT `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` TRUE 70 14 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` TRUE 70 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Never lived together before: the subsection does not begin.
#ASSERT `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` FALSE 100 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 143(1) -- the person responsible`

-- (a): the child lives with him in the week, or is treated as living with him by (2).
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS TRUE

-- (b): contributing at a weekly rate "not less than" the child benefit rate.
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)` 10 10 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)` 20 10 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)` 9.99 10 EQUALS FALSE

-- (1): (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `s 143(1) the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person in the week` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(1) the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person in the week` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(1) the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person in the week` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(1) the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person in the week` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Contributions "over and above" the rate that (1)(b) requires (fork F5): strictly above.
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` 10 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` 10.01 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` 5 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 144(3) -- two or more persons would be entitled`

-- Arguments: how many would be entitled apart from this subsection; the Schedule 10 answer for this person.
#ASSERT `s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled` 2 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "one of them only shall be entitled": Schedule 10 picks another.
#ASSERT `s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled` 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled` 3 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Schedule 10's answer is not known.
#ASSERT `s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled` 2 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Fewer than two: the subsection does not arise.
#ASSERT `s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled` 1 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled` 0 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 145 -- rate of child benefit`

#ASSERT `s 145(1) the weekly rate of child benefit in pounds` (JUST 25) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `s 145(1) the weekly rate of child benefit in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4): no rate prescribed in place of a rate previously in force shall be lower than it.
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the rate prescribed may be lower than the rate it replaces` 10 11 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same or higher: the subsection does not say they are lawful.
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the rate prescribed may be lower than the rate it replaces` 11 11 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145(4) the rate prescribed may be lower than the rate it replaces` 12 11 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 146 -- presence in Great Britain`

#ASSERT `s 146(1) the child or qualifying young person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 146(1) the child or qualifying young person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 146(2) the person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 146(2) the person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 141 -- entitlement to child benefit`

-- Arguments: s 143(1) responsible; s 146(1) child in GB; s 146(2) person in GB; Schedule 9 excludes;
-- persons who would be entitled apart from s 144(3); the Schedule 10 answer.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Two would be entitled and Schedule 10 picks this person.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 2 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Two would be entitled and Schedule 10 picks the other: "one of them only".
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Schedule 10's answer is not known and is needed.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 2 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Schedule 9 excludes entitlement.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The child is not in Great Britain.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The person is not in Great Britain.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not responsible: outside the limit of the grant, so no answer from this section.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- A bar that the Act states beats an unknown elsewhere.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A bar that is unknown leaves the answer unknown.
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 1 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING 1 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING 1 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 145A -- entitlement after the death of a child or qualifying young person`

-- (1) Arguments: the child died; the person was entitled for the week of death; the week asked about, counting
-- the week after the death as 1; the length of the prescribed period in weeks.
#ASSERT `s 145A(1) the person is entitled to child benefit for the week after the death` TRUE TRUE 1 8 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145A(1) the person is entitled to child benefit for the week after the death` TRUE TRUE 8 8 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- After the prescribed period.
#ASSERT `s 145A(1) the person is entitled to child benefit for the week after the death` TRUE TRUE 9 8 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The week of death itself is not "following that week".
#ASSERT `s 145A(1) the person is entitled to child benefit for the week after the death` TRUE TRUE 0 8 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145A(1) the person is entitled to child benefit for the week after the death` FALSE TRUE 1 8 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145A(1) the person is entitled to child benefit for the week after the death` TRUE FALSE 1 8 EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5) "married couple": a man and a woman, married to each other, neither separated by court order nor permanently.
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) "civil partnership".
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a civil partnership` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a civil partnership` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a civil partnership` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a civil partnership` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) "cohabiting couple": not married or civil partners, but living together as if.
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a cohabiting couple` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a cohabiting couple` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a cohabiting couple` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145A(5) the two people are a cohabiting couple` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) Arguments: the person entitled under (1) died before the period's end; married couple; civil partnership;
-- cohabiting couple; he was living with the person he was married to or the civil partner.
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Married but not living with the spouse, and not cohabiting: no answer.
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A member of a cohabiting couple needs no "living with".
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- None of the three: no answer.
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The first person did not die before the period's end.
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Unknown couple status stays unknown, unless another limb is known to hold.
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 145A(3) subsections (1) and (2) apply as if the person were the one who would have been entitled had the child been alive at the beginning of the week` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145A(3) subsections (1) and (2) apply as if the person were the one who would have been entitled had the child been alive at the beginning of the week` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145A(4) section 77 applies with the omission of subsections (4) to (6)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145A(4) section 77 applies with the omission of subsections (4) to (6)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 144(2) -- Schedule 9`

-- Schedule 9 "shall have effect for excluding entitlement": its answer, when it excludes, is the text's own.
#ASSERT `s 144(2) entitlement to child benefit is excluded by Schedule 9` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 144(2) entitlement to child benefit is excluded by Schedule 9` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 144(2) entitlement to child benefit is excluded by Schedule 9` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
